'''''Narcissus serotinus''''' is a autumn-flowering species of the genus ''[[Narcissus (plant)|Narcissus]]'' (daffodils) in the family [[Amaryllidaceae]]. It is classified in Section ''Serotini''. It is native to [[Portugal]], [[Spain]], and [[Morocco]].<ref name="powo">{{cite web |title=Narcissus serotinus L. |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:66213-1 |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew |access-date=21 January 2024}}</ref> Records further east in the Mediterranean refer to ''[[Narcissus obsoletus]]'' and ''[[Narcissus elegans]]''.<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Díaz Lifante |first1=Z. |last2=Camacho |first2=C.A. |title=Morphological variation of Narcissus serotinus L. s.l. (Amaryllidaceae) in the Iberian Peninsula |journal=Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society |date=2007 |volume=154 |issue=2 |pages=237–257 |doi=10.1111/j.1095-8339.2007.00653.x}}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |last1=Díaz Lifante |first1=Z. |last2=Camacho |first2=C.A. |last3=Viruel |first3=J. |last4=Cabrera Caballero |first4=A. |title=The allopolyploid origin of Narcissus obsoletus (Alliaceae): identification of parental genomes by karyotype characterization and genomic in situ hybridization |journal=Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society |date=2009 |volume=159 |pages=477–498 |doi=10.1111/j.1095-8339.2009.00951.x}}</ref>

== Description ==
''Narcissus serotinus'' has one of the smallest [[Perianth#Corona|coronas]] of the genus (see illustration). The flowers are fragrant, the [[tepals]] white and the small corona yellow.

